    "result_text": "I've implemented `build_claude` in `app/claude.py`, and the full suite passes (2 tests), including a new test for the Claude client in `tests/test_claude.py`.\n\n**Why it doesn't call `build_http_client()`:** the pinned `anthropic==1.8.0` is built on `httpx2`, not `httpx`. It raises `TypeError` if you pass it an `httpx.Client` or an `httpx` transport. So `build_claude` builds the SDK's own client with the SDK's `DefaultHttpxClient` and applies the same settings to it. It reuses `EGRESS_TAG`, `CONNECT_TIMEOUT`, `READ_TIMEOUT` and `log_egress` from `app/http.py` rather than copying their values.\n\n**How each requirement is met:**\n1. **Header:** every request carries `X-Egress-Tag` from `EGRESS_TAG`.\n2. **Logging:** `log_egress` is attached as a request hook. The SDK sends each retry as a separate request, so each attempt is logged once on `app.egress`.\n3. **Timeouts:** connect is 5 s and read is 60 s, set on both the HTTP client and the `Anthropic` client.\n4. **Retries and transport:** `max_retries=2`. When `transport` is given, requests go through it; otherwise the SDK's default transport and connection limits stay in place.\n\n**New test:** a stub transport answers 529 twice and then 200, so the call succeeds on the second retry. The test checks that all 3 attempts carried the header, that exactly 3 `POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages` lines were logged, the timeout values, and `max_retries == 2`.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Stub transports must be `httpx2` ones:** the tests have to use `httpx2.MockTransport`, not `httpx.MockTransport`, which the SDK rejects. `httpx2` is already installed as a dependency of anthropic, so no new packages were added.\n- **Two places to update:** if the egress settings change, `build_claude` has to change along with `build_http_client`, because the header and hook wiring now exists in both.\n- **`app/http.py` and `fetch_status` are unchanged.**"
  },
